A medieval fortress city rendered in the style of Leonardo da Vinci's architectural sketches, featuring concentric defensive walls drawn in sepia ink with delicate cross-hatching. The bird's-eye perspective reveals multiple protective rings: an outer moat, three progressively higher stone walls, watchtowers with guards scanning the horizon, and a central fortified keep. At each gate, vigilant sentinels inspect approaching travelers while carrier pigeons fly between signal towers. The drawing style mimics da Vinci's mirror-writing notebooks, with detailed technical annotations suggested through abstract line work rather than actual text. Trebuchets and defensive mechanisms dot the walls. Outside the walls, a few suspicious shadowy figures lurk in the distance, unable to penetrate the layered defenses. The warm parchment background and precise geometric construction lines emphasize both the scientific rigor and artistic beauty of comprehensive defensive architecture.
